          icon: "🎭",
          term: { zh: "贝尔宾团队角色", en: "Belbin Team Roles" },
          level: 2,
          oneLiner: {
            zh: "高效团队不靠凑明星，而靠角色互补：把思考、协作、行动三类的八种角色各就各位。",
            en: "A strong team is not a pile of stars but complementary roles — the eight varieties of thinking, social and action each filled.",
          },
          detail: {
            zh: "梅雷迪思·贝尔宾通过长期团队观察提出：一个人的贡献不只看他的专业与职位，更要看他天然愿意、也擅长承担的“团队角色”。经典八种归为三类——思考型（智多星出创意与点子，监督评估者冷静审度利弊、把关方向）、人际型（协调者定方向、善用人才，资源探索者对外搜寻机会与情报，团队工作者维系关系、润滑协作）、行动型（推进者施压破除障碍、追求速度，实干家把想法落成可执行的计划，完善者紧盯细节、防止疏漏、保障交付）。要点不是给每人贴上一个固定标签，而是让角色配置互补、避免扎堆：全是点子王就没人收尾，全是执行机器则缺乏方向，全是和事佬则难以作硬决定。后来他又补入第九种“专家”（某一领域难得的深度专长），并强调允许成员在需要时临时承担自己不优先的角色以补位。",
            en: "Meredith Belbin, from long observation of teams, argued that a person's contribution lies not just in expertise or title but in the team role they naturally will and can play. The classic eight fall into three clusters — thinking (the Plant generates ideas, the Monitor-Evaluator weighs pros and coolly guards direction), social (the Co-ordinator sets direction and uses people well, the Resource Investigator scouts opportunity and intelligence outside, the Teamworker holds relationships and smooths collaboration) and action (the Shaper pressures through obstacles for speed, the Implementer turns ideas into workable plans, the Completer-Finisher watches detail, prevents slips and guards delivery). The point is not to pin a fixed label on everyone but to balance the mix so roles complement and do not pile up: a team of idea-machines never finishes, a team of doers lacks direction, a team of harmonisers cannot make hard calls. He later added a ninth, the Specialist for rare depth in one field, and urged letting members take a non-preferred role temporarily to fill a gap.",
          },
