            zh: "外科医生阿图·葛文德发现：现代工作的失败常非因无知，而在“知道却漏做”——复杂性、不确定性与时间压力压垮了人的记忆与疏忽防线。他借航空业“起飞前检查清单”的成功，为世界卫生组织设计了手术安全清单（切皮前核对身份、部位、过敏、备血、团队沟通），在多国八家医院试点，术后死亡率与并发症显著下降。要点很克制：清单只列“关键、易漏”的少数几项，分清“检查—确认”（做完再打勾）与“朗读—执行”（边读边做）两类流程，绝不写成百科；更要配套“照单办事、也敢于叫停”的文化，否则清单沦为走过场。它是把已知变成“必然被做”的低成本、高杠杆工具，也适用于系统上线、交接、急诊与软件开发。",
            en: "Surgeon Atul Gawande found that modern failure is often not ignorance but knowing and still missing it — complexity, uncertainty and time pressure overwhelm memory and our defences against slips. Borrowing aviation's pre-flight checklist he designed, for the World Health Organization, a surgical safety checklist (confirming identity, site, allergies, blood and team communication before the cut), piloted in eight hospitals across countries, where deaths and complications fell markedly. The craft is deliberately spare: list only the few critical, easily-skipped items, distinguish do-confirmation (tick after doing) from read-do (act as you read), and never write an encyclopaedia; above all pair it with a culture of following the list yet daring to halt, or it degrades into ritual. It is a low-cost, high-leverage way to turn what is known into what reliably gets done, and it fits go-lives, handoffs, emergencies and software too.",
