          level: 3,
          oneLiner: {
            zh: "雇佣关系里那份“没写进合同”的相互期待:一旦违背,失望与疏离先于任何条款。",
            en: "The unwritten mutual expectations of employment — breach them and disappointment and withdrawal come before any clause.",
          },
          detail: {
            zh: "概念由组织行为学家阿基里斯提出、后经丹尼斯·卢梭推广：“心理契约”是员工与组织之间未曾成文、却彼此默认的期待交换（忠诚换稳定、努力换发展与公平、服从换“照看”与庇护）。它没有任何签字，却在每一天的互动中被“履行”或“违背”：公司突然裁员、承诺的晋升或调薪不兑现、“加班无回报”“说好的培养没下文”，都会被员工体验为心理契约破裂，继而知觉为违背，直接侵蚀信任、敬业度与组织公民行为，拉低绩效、引发消极怠工乃至离职与报复。管理要点是招聘与带人时别过度承诺、开明沟通期望、变化尽早透明、失约后及时解释与补偿；期望对齐是一种低成本的信任投资，一旦透支却极难修复。",
            en: "Coined by the organisational behaviourist Argyris and advanced by Denise Rousseau, the psychological contract is the unwritten, mutually assumed exchange of expectations between employee and organisation — loyalty for security, effort for development and fairness, deference for being looked after and protected. Signed nowhere, it is nonetheless honoured or breached in daily interaction: sudden layoffs, promised promotions or raises that never arrive, unpaid overtime, mentoring that quietly lapses — all are experienced as breach and then perceived as violation, eroding trust, engagement and organisational citizenship, lowering performance and breeding quiet withdrawal or even exit and retaliation. The managerial rule is not to overpromise in hiring and managing, to talk expectations out in the open, to make change transparent early, and after a broken promise to explain and make amends promptly; aligning expectations is a low-cost investment in trust that, once overdrawn, is very hard to repair.",
          },
          tags: [{ zh: "关系", en: "Relations" }],
          related: ["psych-safety", "org-culture", "engagement-q12"],
